{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"847","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Dog Show"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A new dog show on TV is starting next week. On the show dogs are required to demonstrate bottomless stomach, strategic thinking and self-preservation instinct. You and your dog are invited to compete with other participants and naturally you want to win!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the show a dog needs to eat as many bowls of dog food as possible (bottomless stomach helps here). Dogs compete separately of each other and the rules are as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the start of the show the dog and the bowls are located on a line. The dog starts at position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" bowls are located at positions "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x = 1, x = 2, ..., x = n"},{"kind":"text","text":". The bowls are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" from left to right. After the show starts the dog immediately begins to run to the right to the first bowl."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The food inside bowls is not ready for eating at the start because it is too hot (dog's self-preservation instinct prevents eating). More formally, the dog can eat from the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bowl after "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds from the start of the show or later."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It takes dog 1 second to move from the position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". The dog is not allowed to move to the left, the dog runs only to the right with the constant speed 1 distance unit per second. When the dog reaches a bowl (say, the bowl "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the following cases are possible:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the food had cooled down (i.e. it passed at least "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds from the show start): the dog immediately eats the food and runs to the right without any stop, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the food is hot (i.e. it passed less than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds from the show start): the dog has two options: to wait for the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bowl, eat the food and continue to run at the moment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" or to skip the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bowl and continue to run to the right without any stop. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds from the start the show ends. If the dog reaches a bowl of food at moment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" the dog can not eat it. The show stops before "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds if the dog had run to the right of the last bowl."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You need to help your dog create a strategy with which the maximum possible number of bowls of food will be eaten in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two integer numbers are given in the first line - "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 200 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ T ≤ 2·109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of bowls of food and the time when the dog is stopped."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the next line numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t1, t2, ..., tn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ti ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") are given, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the moment of time when the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bowl of food is ready for eating."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the maximum number of bowls of food the dog will be able to eat in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 5\n1 5 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example the dog should skip the second bowl to eat from the two bowls (the first and the third)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"847D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/847/problem/D"}